& [FixtureRegistration] admits one exact closed evidence set
  + the fixture binds distinct before and projected candidate generations, their exact predecessor relation, one compiler impact, source and target artifacts, correspondence records, proof media, and eight required diff kinds
  + every content input is digest verified, role categorized, count bounded, nonempty, and disjoint across SOP source, SemanticIR, BuildIR, target metadata, forward correspondence, independent correspondence, and proof media
  + source, semantic, target, correspondence, proof, and unrelated-preservation references must exist in the supplied closed set
  + registration inserts only supplied immutable forms and bytes, rebuilds the repository index, and validates the resulting root

& [ForwardPass] derives a committed prediction
  + the forward pass reads the projected candidate generation and compiler impact rather than the rear diff records
  + it derives changed sources, invalidations, dependencies, target artifacts, diagnostics, proof requirements, and explicit unknowns in normalized order
  + the prediction carries a digest over its exact fixture identity and derived result

& [RearPass] is independent and comparative
  + the rear pass derives observed source and semantic changes, invalidations, unknowns, and preserved unrelated identities from the complete eight-kind DiffRecord set
  + rear evidence must be distinct from every forward evidence role
  + comparison records whether forward and rear results match without laundering a mismatch into success
  + mismatch invalidates the projected candidate, forward prediction, candidate targets, and all predicted or observed invalidations while retaining the rear record as evidence and preserving unrelated identities

& [ProofCheckedGeneration] preserves immutable identity
  + successful checking requires an exact forward and rear match, complete diffs, independent evidence, and a current Observer Admit or Qualify join
  + the Observer subject set must name the projected candidate, requested proof-checked generation, impact, prediction, rear comparison, all diff records, independent evidence, and proof bundle
  + checking never mutates the projected candidate generation
  + checking emits a distinct proof_checked CompilerGeneration whose exact predecessor is the projected candidate and binds it to the fixture record

& [DeterministicRootAndFaultBoundary] is reconstructable
  + root validation recomputes content digests, role partitions, repository indexes, generation ancestry, impact and diff bindings, prediction and rear digests, status-specific references, and invalidation and preservation disjointness
  + wrong generation, incomplete diff, missing correspondence, missing reference, invalid form, digest mismatch, duplicate identity, bound violation, and Observer mismatch remain typed refusals
  + every accepted operation returns an immutable successor and receipt; every refusal leaves the supplied root unchanged

& [DeliberateLimits] are binding
  + this is a fixed in-memory compiler fixture and not a parser, general compiler, target backend, optimizer, learned model, database service, or execution provider
  + the operation surface performs no filesystem, Git, network, process, clock, thread, notification, device, FPGA, or hardware effect
  + supplied content bytes and form records are test data, not authority derived from ambient files

